{"message":"feat(tactics): close constructor contradictions with compact literal proofs\n\nSearch local empty evidence, negations and nested constructor equalities\nusing ordinary recursors and equality transports. Use admitted Nat.beq\nfor huge literal disequalities without unary successor expansion. Pin\nmemoized endpoint allocations and retain scope and checking obligations.\n\nSeven additional source tests and a real installed CLI test pass locally,\nincluding 129-bit literals, proof-family refusals and injection followed\nby dependent subst. Scoped Clippy and workspace compilation pass. Remote\npublication reruns all five packages before committing production code.","paths":["crates/fln-cli/tests/source_check.rs","crates/fln-elab/src/source/tactics.rs","crates/fln-elab/src/source/tactics/constructors.rs","crates/fln-parse/src/proofs.rs","crates/fln/tests/source_constructor_equality.rs","docs/NATIVE_CONSTRUCTOR_EQUALITY.md","examples/native_constructor_equality.lean"],"sha256":"dc2d33933abc24d5d744b2c55e0b1cdf2c78792ebb22750093b014dbbc8c3b47","patch_gzip_base64":""}